# One canonical representation, everywhere.
#
# Without this file, Git on Windows checks text out as CRLF and on Linux/macOS as
# LF. That is normally harmless. It was not harmless here, because
# tools/Build-CoverageRegister.ps1 MEASURES FILE SIZES: CRLF adds one byte per
# line, 66 of 144 topics changed size between the authoring machine and the CI
# runner, and the coverage gate failed for two days against a register that was
# correct. The generator has since been made line-ending independent - this file
# closes the same hole from the other side.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` means: Git decides what is text, stores LF in the object
# database (it always did), and checks LF out on every platform. PowerShell,
# pwsh, and every editor in use here read LF without complaint.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicit for the file types this repo actually contains, so the intent survives
# someone changing the wildcard above.
*.md    text eol=lf
*.ps1   text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.kql   text eol=lf
*.bicep text eol=lf

# Never touch these.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.gif   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.zip   binary
